          "python": "# A complete mini machine-learning project: data, a model, training and an honest test.\nimport random\n\nrandom.seed(7)\n# Made-up data: hours of practice -> typing speed (words per minute), with noise.\ndata = [(h, round(20 + 6 * h + random.uniform(-4, 4), 1)) for h in range(0, 11)]\nrandom.shuffle(data)\ntrain, test = data[:8], data[8:]\n\nw, b, rate = 0.0, 0.0, 0.01\nfor step in range(2000):\n    dw = sum(2 * (w * x + b - y) * x for x, y in train) / len(train)\n    db = sum(2 * (w * x + b - y) for x, y in train) / len(train)\n    w, b = w - rate * dw, b - rate * db\n\ndef mse(examples, predict):\n    return sum((predict(x) - y) ** 2 for x, y in examples) / len(examples)\n\nmean_y = sum(y for _, y in train) / len(train)\nprint(f\"learned: speed = {w:.2f} * hours + {b:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"test error, model:    {mse(test, lambda x: w * x + b):7.2f}\")\nprint(f\"test error, baseline: {mse(test, lambda x: mean_y):7.2f}  (always predict the average)\")\nprint(f\"prediction for 12 hours: {w * 12 + b:.0f} wpm\")\n"
