          "python": "first tickets: [3, 10, 17, 24, 31, 38] ... last 444\nfind  10 -> linear: index  1 in  2 probes | binary: index  1 in 5 probe(s)\nfind 290 -> linear: index 41 in 42 probes | binary: index 41 in 5 probe(s)\nfind 444 -> linear: index 63 in 64 probes | binary: index 63 in 7 probe(s)\nfind 100 -> linear: index -1 in 64 probes | binary: index -1 in 6 probe(s)\nlog2(64) = 6, so binary search never needs more than 7 probes here."
