            "python": "sort [5, 1, 4, 2, 8, 3]:\n  pass 1: [1, 4, 2, 5, 3, 8]\n  pass 2: [1, 2, 4, 3, 5, 8]\n  pass 3: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8]\n  pass 4: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 8]\n  passes=4 comparisons=14 swaps=7\nnearly sorted [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 6, 8, 9, 10]:\n  passes=2 comparisons=17 swaps=1\nreversed (worst case):\n  passes=9 comparisons=45 swaps=45"
